# Resolution
Fixed in https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/8b45d67d3e1ff591a8937a7962242a03c10f8953.

The control-plane RPC decoder now validates nested collection counts against
the remaining bounded frame payload before allocating collection capacity. The
fix applies to heartbeat PG observations, runtime-map nodes, runtime-map PG
routes, and PG route acting sets. Oversized counts now fail with
ControlPlaneError::RpcProtocol before Vec::with_capacity is called.

Regression coverage added:
- control_plane_rpc_rejects_oversized_heartbeat_observation_count_before_allocation
- control_plane_rpc_rejects_oversized_runtime_node_count_before_allocation
- control_plane_rpc_rejects_oversized_runtime_route_count_before_allocation
- control_plane_rpc_rejects_oversized_runtime_acting_set_count_before_allocation

